ition  maybe just because somebody said oh he's  a philosopher they thought that that's  where he would wind up  but of course i agree um with the points  that both the previous speakers have  have made  hannah gave especially good examples of  uh misuse of of formalities and rituals  and uh linda uh uh actually anticipated  a number of the things i was going to  say about uh the uh power of ritual to  uh foster attention uh focusing and and  fortification um uh as uh uh uh uh will  become evident uh i think of rituals  especially in terms of their capacity to  cause um emotional unity uh  as as a means of of attention and uh  focus and fortification thanks  thank you so much to our speakers for  laying out their position there now  let's dive straight into it  our traditions have been long-standing  and we do things a certain way be they  due to customs morality or religion  we're speaking here from uh the united  kingdom where um to be knighted is to be  united by the royal family in a very uh  ritualistic process which some might  argue uh reinforces social class by um  rendering certain groups within society  able to uh bestow certain honors over  others and elevate them as it were  socially and economically but rituals  mark key moments in our lives be they  marriage or funeral  to continue watching this video click  the link in the top left or in the  description below or visit iai dot tv  for more debates and talks from the  world's leading thinkers on today's  biggest ideas

